`KSpecC4`: the per-link obligation in the shape of `KSpecC512` (the registers the avx_x1 link
reads at entry, `L1 = WinAvxX1Live.live_entry_eq`, include the Win64 callee-saved registers it
pushes; the avx_x4 stream never writes them, `avx_x4_callee_gpr_untouched`).  The hand-off log
carries the kernel's frame cells (`sub rsp, 568`), hence depth 568.

`TurnOut4` (R2c): the output bytes of R2's W-mode avx_x4 loop certificate
`AvxX4LoopWAll.x4_runW`, stated against exactly its run.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

